# A value-used model method is an LMX value in an ordinary unit. It must not
# acquire a public C prototype under its source name: div collides with libc.
# The method's graph-callable body stays behind its internal l2_mK symbol.
fn: div (int: y; int: x) int
    return: y + x

fn: wrap (int: k) fn: (int: x) int
    return: merge(div; y: k)

@: f wrap(5)
int: result (f: 2)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: result; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
